WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:18.320
Shiro High put on 
quite a performance.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.660
Yeah, they're outta sight.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.330
Seriously.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.460
We can't even compare...

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.580
Er, just kidding! There's no contest!

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.240
They don't stand a chance! Right, Captain?

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.400
Captain?

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.040
Aw, chicken?

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.680
No Sendai beef?

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:59.200
You think I'd put in that pricey crap?

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.380
Mashiro, mind your manners.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.710
Is there anything we can do to help?

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.220
No, it's all ready.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.210
Did you finish getting your rooms in order?

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.570
I'm sorry about that.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.340
I meant to clean them before you got here...

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.080
No, it's our fault for showing up early.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:25.600
A gift for you.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.100
<b>Whole Apples
Kininaru Ringo</b>

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.020
An Aomori specialty, Kininaru Ringo!

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.020
<b>Whole Apples
Kininaru Ringo</b>

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.780
Of course, it's apples.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.540
Hey, Brief-kun.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.780
"Brief-kun"?!

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.760
I taught him all about it!

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.450
Please don't go teaching people that!

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.330
My name is Shotaro Futaba.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.450
Shotaro Futaba...

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.460
Futacchi? Soartaro?

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.920
Is Misa-pon not here?

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.720
Misato-kun commutes from home.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:57.960
What are these?

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:01.220
Sasa kamaboko.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.740
Sasa kamaboko?

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:14.640
Hey, Mashiro!

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.860
That's good!

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:16.740
You think so?

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.530
Then try this one.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.010
It's still in its trial phase...

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:23.620
Grated apple curry flavor!

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.910
I guess you like apples, too.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.790
Do <i>not</i>. This ain't apple flavor.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.500
It's grated apple <i>curry</i>!

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.250
Like I said, apple.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.260
It's <i>curry</i> flavor!

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.250
Apple!

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.120
It's curry, I'm tellin' you!

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:36.670
Apple!

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:37.380
Curry!

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.080
So good!

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.080
Apple!

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.010
Curry!

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:08.930
<b><i>Backflip!!</i></b>

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.290
Shichigahama.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.880
Time to wake up.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:24.280
Yeah...

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:30.740
Morning.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.250
Mornin'!

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.540
Good morning!

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:36.370
Morning.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.320
Good morning.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.420
Misato-kun! Good morning.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.780
Hey there, Early Riser Ace.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.840
Don't call me that.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.540
Wait, wasn't the front door locked?

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.450
We unlocked it for him.

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:55.350
Takase!

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.820
What do you mean, you unlocked it for him?!

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.460
We woke up pretty early, you know.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.130
Then we went for a little jog.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:07.560
We started on the cleaning. Breakfast, too.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.140
Hope we're not imposing.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:16.480
Wh-What the hell is this?!

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.460
Wow, it's sparkling.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:20.480
Who's on hall cleaning duty today?

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.850
Oh, that's me.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:24.550
Chesto!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.490
Chesto, chesto, chesto, chesto, chesto!

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.300
U-Um...

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:34.630
Chesto, chesto, chesto, chesto, chesto!

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.880
Excuse me! I'm supposed to...

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:36.060
Hold it, you!

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:41.150
Chesto-to-to-to-to-to!

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.580
U-Um!

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.550
Hey!

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:46.980
When a man's talkin', you'd better listen!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.790
The month of May...

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.790
In Iwanuma, that means peonies.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.070
Such a lovely bloom.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.220
Beautiful...

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:06.800
What?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.360
It's still a little thin.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.810
I must have misjudged the moisture 
expelled from the vegetables.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.320
You sonuva bitch!

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.070
Musclin' in on a man's turf!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.490
Add 0.2 grams of amino acid, then salt...

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.450
Hey! Look at me, ya punk!

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:35.080
Watari! Calm down!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.120
Captain!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.330
Lemme go, bro!

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.240
Cut it out!

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.290
He's musclin' in on my turf!

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.490
Adjustments complete. It's delicious.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.320
Watari! Calm down!

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:46.820
Lemme go! I'mma murder his ass!

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.520
So ordered! Go forth, Watari!

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:49.840
Captain?!

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:59.370
A full evaluation of the precision 
and beauty of your basic movements,

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:03.480
as well as your synchronization as a group.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:07.600
That's what we're going for 
here at this year's training camp.

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:08.600
Yes, sir!

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:20.100
Stay mindful of your whole body, 
from your head to your toes!

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.490
Don't slack off just because it's practice!

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:23.420
Yes, sir!

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:26.370
Point those toes!

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.420
Yes, sir!

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.530
You there! You're looking shaky!

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:39.770
Yes, sir!

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.350
Don't sway all over the place!

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.460
If you wanna move, you should be dancing!

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:44.900
Sorry, sir!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.080
Okay, next up is tumbling!

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:52.050
Keep it snappy! Let's see those moves!

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:52.920
Sir!

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:59.330
Don't be afraid to put 'em 
through their paces yourself.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.060
I'm not, Mabuchi-senpai.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:05.120
I'm just bad at explaining things to people.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:10.340
"I don't have time to waste 
on rock-bottom dregs."

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:15.950
To think the man who once said that
 would become a teacher...

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:18.340
Gosh, what an embarrassing reminder.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:23.640
What?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:27.300
You mean Coach Shida and Coach Mabuchi...

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:31.070
Yeah. They're Hakumei University alumni.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:34.550
They laid the foundation for Hakumei's 
men's rhythmic gymnastics team.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:36.110
They're legendary.

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:43.710
Return to article

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.710
That's our coach?

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:47.250
He seems so different now.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:50.210
That look in his eyes... 
He's one helluva fighter.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:53.440
He used to be Hakumei University's ace.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.780
Curious about an aces of old, 
New Hotness Ace?

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.360
Don't call me that.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:11.020
Return to article

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:08.530
The system designed 
to provide rigorous training

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:11.340
across seven years at Hakumei's 
high school and then university

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.030
was developed during his time there.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.120
In other words, he's that good.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.140
No time for gawking.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.220
We've got a serious performance ahead of us 
at the university this afternoon.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.970
Let's nail the sucker 
and show 'em what we're all about!

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:30.640
Right!

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:30.640
Got it!

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:34.050
<b>Sekiou University</b>

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.040
You shoulda come to Shiro High 
with me, Misa-pon.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:52.100
We coulda had even more fun 
and done cool things together.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:54.880
Oh well.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:01.970
It's fun to compete on different teams, too.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.580
<b>Drive\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDedication\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hCourage!!</b>

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.680
Each school will now perform.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.550
If something sticks out,

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:16.660
the other team should feel free
 to offer critiques and advice.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.910
Everyone ready?
 Let's give it everything we got.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.860
Mutsu, jump high and hard.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:26.810
Ominato, keep your face loose and expressive.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.460
Azuma, unleash your top speed.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.650
Ryugamori, show off 
that flexibility of yours.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.860
Mashiro, don't play around just 
because this is a training camp.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:38.480
I want your all out there.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:39.840
Right.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.620
Watch what your teammates are doing closely.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.830
Let's keep ourselves in sync!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:47.800
Right!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:47.800
Yah!

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.650
We'll start with Shiro High.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:52.600
Yes, sir!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:11.980
Shiro High sure is something...

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:21.210
How are <i>we</i> supposed critique <i>that</i>?

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:24.160
<b>Kawamura</b>

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.560
If I'm honest, I'm pretty disappointed.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:31.540
I have to wonder why we came 
all the way to Miyagi.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.640
Good point.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.930
Are they really so 
worthy of our attention?

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:47.120
Yeah, don't bother.

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:53.360
A performance like that 
don't deserve feedback.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.860
<b>Kawamura</b>

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:03.660
I first saw Ao High perform two years ago.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:08.240
There was a joint practice 
for the six Tohoku prefectures.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:09.980
And there...

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.540
Soshukan High School?

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:19.050
Sounds like their team 
is brand new this year.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:35.240
Their performance was spectacular.

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:38.400
It was clear how much they'd practiced.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:41.820
And last year at the 
Miyagi Prefecture Tournament,

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:45.440
they scored a shocking 15 points 
with only four men.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.440
<b>70th Miyagi Prefecture Inter-High Athletics Tournament
Men's Rhythmic Gymnastics</b>

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.440
<b>Soshukan High School</b>

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.900
I'm telling you,
 they'll crawl their way up.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:55.580
How come we can't get ourselves
 in sync with six men?

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:59.280
Maybe the four of us are 
so used to performing together

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:02.800
that we're not minding Misato and Shotaro.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.360
Coach...

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.150
I'm sorry!

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.350
Captain...

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:20.460
You put together this training camp for us,

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:22.880
and we put on that pathetic display!

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:28.300
Isn't the sky so clear and beautiful?

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:35.120
Sometimes it's nice 
to just stand still and look up at it.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.960
That's what my wife says.

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:40.710
The sky?

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.220
Good work today.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:50.820
There'll be more tomorrow, 
so make sure you rest up.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.280
Thinking about Mashiro?

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:06.320
It's pointless.

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:10.210
He's a prodigy. You aren't.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:11.740
But...

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:15.080
"Don't run yourself ragged 
to compete with a prodigy!"

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.420
"Just go at your own pace!"

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:21.540
Is that what you're trying 
to say, Inarticulate Ace?

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.920
Don't call me that.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:25.920
It's not like that.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:31.340
I'm not trying to be like Mashiro-kun.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:37.520
I just want to be able to keep up 
so that I'm not dragging you guys down.

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:42.900
So I was wondering if maybe 
I could learn something from him.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.900
Sounds like running yourself ragged to me.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:47.870
Yup, yup!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.930
Don't you worry. We'll adjust 
our performance to match you.

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:55.980
Same to you, Misato...

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:59.350
But I guess you don't have 
to worry about that.

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:04.690
Yeah. I think Misato's the one 
holding back to match <i>us</i>.

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:05.780
I don't think so.

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.340
Keeping up with us...

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.920
Holding back to match us...

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:27.420
Anyway, let's work hard 
to get ourselves in sync tomorrow—

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.480
Screw gettin' in sync!

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:31.660
Shichigahama?

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.780
Shotaro's a freakin' newbie!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:37.520
Misato hasn't known us long.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:41.590
And the rest of us are too used 
to our four-man routine!

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:42.710
So...

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.120
Of course!

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.260
We're all trying too hard 
to match each other.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.960
We're so focused on each other

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.970
that we're neglecting our own movements.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.410
What are we doin' this for?

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:57.390
It's to get to the Inter-High!

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.350
Not to all move the same way!

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:05.050
Shotaro, quit thinkin' 
about catchin' up to us.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:08.740
From now on, focus on surpassin' us!

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.610
We're on the same team, sure. But...

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:15.190
We're also rivals!

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:16.900
Same to you, Misato.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.040
Don't go holdin' back for our sakes.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:22.510
Give it all you got!

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:25.500
Rivals?

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:30.950
My senpais and I... are rivals?

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:35.260
All six of us need to set our sights higher.

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:40.670
All six of us need
 to aim for even greater heights!

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:43.440
Let's do this!

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.440
Yeah!

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:48.150
Hey! It's Misa-pon!

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.700
Mashiro?

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.300
Takase?

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:57.460
The six of us are climbin' higher.

00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:03.770
Higher than where you stand right now!

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:08.440
Then we'll just have to knock you back down.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:11.550
Speaking of,

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:15.190
now that we have a full team of six,
there's something important we kinda forgot.

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:16.620
Something important?

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:20.350
We've got the Shiro High guys here, too.

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:24.610
Let's all get together and do this right!

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.900
<b>Welcome, Shiro High<i>!!</i>
Welcome, New Members<i>!!</i></b>

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:36.990
See?!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.660
Ma-chan puts her soul into her work!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.260
Her zeal for practice, 
her love for her fans...

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:44.410
She's so pure!

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:48.850
Tan-Tan Girls. Masami Kudo. 
Nineteen years old.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:50.880
Height: 159 centimeters.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.320
Blood type: A.

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:53.720
Image color: pink.

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:55.240
Special talent: violin.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.840
Are you...

00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:02.600
I'm a fan of Aki Kazamaura, 
from Aomori Nebuta Dream.

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.600
<i>Hakumei University Private</i>

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.600
<i>Student Notebook
</i>

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.600
<i>Hakumei</i>

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:09.100
Ma-chan! Ma-chan! Ma-chan!

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:12.610
Why... Why, bro?!

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:13.070
<b>Battles Without 
Morals 
and Humanity</b>

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:15.800
You promised!

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.720
You promised we'd cross 
that bridge together!

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:21.030
We're livin' in a new era.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:25.580
Those dreams of ours have long rusted away...

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:28.570
Just like that bridge.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.170
Apple-moss?

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.190
Yes. I call him Tamao-san.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:36.710
And this is my green penny fern, Mameko-san.

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:40.110
She's beautiful!

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:42.180
<b>Welcome, Shiro High<i>!!</i>
Welcome, New Members<i>!!</i></b>

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:42.180
What is all this?

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.340
I think it's supposed to be 
your welcome party,

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:47.480
and our getting-to-know-you party.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:50.010
If we place a peony here...

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:52.440
That's incredible, Ryugamori-kun!

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.250
Die!

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.830
Sakai, you... bastard...

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.590
Tan, tan, ta-ta-tan!

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:02.880
This is chaos.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:14.040
Those are some weaksauce 
clumsy backflips, as usual.

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:17.180
And your sasakama-obsessed ass
 reeks of trying too hard.

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:18.320
What was that?!

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.390
My backflips are faster!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.220
It ain't all about speed.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.160
Mine are higher!

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:26.380
Are not!

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:29.180
All right! Let's take this outside!

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.190
You're on!

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.020
Shichigahama!

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:37.400
Our two captains are quite a handful.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:42.240
Speakin' of backflips, 
yours are really on point.

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:45.210
And your pivots are excellent, 
Tsukidate-san.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:46.780
Oh, nah...

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:50.010
That reminds me. 
I've been wanting to ask the room...

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:52.120
Any tips for that oblique front bend move?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.580
You mean like how to time the rebound?

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.590
I have video.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:02.360
First, Tsukidate-senpai's oblique front bend.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.360
What is it?

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:04.800
Wow, outta sight!

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:04.800
You're smiling.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.850
Next, Captain Shichigahama's.

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.860
That extension on his arms!

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:10.370
Everyone just loves 
rhythmic gymnastics so much.

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:10.360
His freehand exercises are amazing.

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:11.930
That's our captain!

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:13.900
Misato-kun, you...

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:18.800
Um, what made you choose Ao High?

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:26.150
This is the only place I can do 
the rhythmic gymnastics I want to do.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.280
That's all.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:34.370
What you want to do...

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:38.340
Where you want to go...

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:05.530
What did you do?

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:09.420
Your kids look a lot sharper today.

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:12.920
Just talked about the sky.

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:16.830
<i>We're all a team.</i>

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.670
<i>We're all rivals.</i>

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:20.460
<i>All of us...</i>

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.040
<i>Even me!</i>
